# ── One commit message, and the reason it is here ───────────────────────
# Commit 859020c removed the author's real username and home path from the
# tree. Its own message quoted the offending string twice while explaining
# which file it came out of, and the gate scans commit messages (11.2), so
# the commit that fixed the leak reported one.
#
# That is 11.1's recorded failure mode for the fourth time in this repo:
# the record of a protected string containing the protected string. It was
# caught by the gate, on the pushed tree, doing exactly its job.
#
# These two entries are the ONLY ones in this file that should be DELETED
# rather than re-pointed after a history squash. Their text lives in a
# commit message and nowhere else, so a squash removes the finding along
# with the message. Re-pointing them to the squashed commit would suppress
# nothing and leave two stale entries behind.

